WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:01.850
- [Princess Margaret] We're being filmed

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:03.990
watching television.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.300
That people might watch
us, watching television,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.563
on their own television sets at home.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.964
- This really is plumbing
new depths of banality.

00:00:14.964 --> 00:00:17.068
- [Presenter] --first
home computer terminal.

00:00:17.068 --> 00:00:19.162
They're simple to operate,
and experts predict

00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:22.250
that in 20 years' time, all
new houses will be built

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.690
with special computer points,

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.720
and that terminals will be cheaper to rent

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.738
than today's telephones.

00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:29.422
- What do we do now?

00:00:29.422 --> 00:00:31.707
- Do you expect us to say something?

00:00:31.707 --> 00:00:32.702
- Yes.

00:00:32.702 --> 00:00:33.774
- Well, what?

00:00:33.774 --> 00:00:35.789
Did someone prepare something?

00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:38.640
- I think the general
idea is it be unscripted,

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.600
to reflect a normal evening.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.150
- This is nothing like a normal evening.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.520
If it was a normal evening,
we'd all be on our own,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.340
in sad isolation, in individual palaces.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.070
We wouldn't be crowded like this,

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.974
this is like some sort
of nightmare Christmas.

00:00:54.974 --> 00:00:55.807
(chuckles)

00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:57.030
- [Presenter] Rex Malek
sees a future world

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.690
where children could be
virtually educated by computer,

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.690
where every home will
have its own terminal,

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:02.990
plugged into a central--

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:05.840
- Ah, perhaps Your Majesties,
Your Royal Highnesses,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.713
perhaps you might comment
on what's on the television?

00:01:09.843 --> 00:01:12.824
- That'd be easier if there were something

00:01:12.824 --> 00:01:14.750
remotely amusing to watch.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.650
- I agree, this is deathly.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.300
- Things might improve with a drink.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.900
- Everything improves with a drink.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:20.750
- Not everything.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.072
- Don't be such a prig.

00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:24.809
Colin!

00:01:24.809 --> 00:01:25.859
- [Director] And cut.

